    {
      "source": "e2",
      "predicate": "said to",
      "target": "e3",
      "evidence": "Bruin began to rub his nose with his disengaged paw, and to look helplessly about him, as he always did when disturbed in mind. \"Now--now--now!\" he exclaimed, \"you hawk, what do you mean by that? Couldn't you dig for roots?\" The hawk stared."
    },
    {
      "source": "e3",
      "predicate": "repeated",
      "target": "e2",
      "evidence": "\"Dig for roots?\" he repeated, contemptuously."
    },
    {
      "source": "e3",
      "predicate": "said to",
      "target": "e4",
      "evidence": "\"Ask that old thing,\" said the hawk, nodding toward the hermit"
    },
    {
      "source": "e2",
      "predicate": "asked",
      "target": "e8",
      "evidence": "Bruin... asked: \"Mr. Baldhead--excuse me! but--a--have you ever tried digging for roots in the ground--with your beak--I mean, nose?\""
    },
    {
      "source": "e4",
      "predicate": "said to",
      "target": "e2",
      "evidence": "\"No, my friend,\" he said with great seriousness, \"I have never tried it...\""
    },
    {
      "source": "e5",
      "predicate": "sat on the knee of",
      "target": "e4",
      "evidence": "The hermit looked up gravely, as he sat with Pigeon Pretty on his knee."
    },
    {
      "source": "e2",
      "predicate": "said to",
      "target": "e3",
      "evidence": "\"I don't see anything for it _but_ to wring your neck, do you? After all, it will keep you from being hungry again.\""
    },
